{
  "_comment": "Allowlist for intentional locale drift, consumed by scripts/check-i18n-keys.mjs.\n\nSchema:\n  {\n    \"missing\":       { <locale>: { <namespace>: [\"dotted.key\", ...] } },\n    \"extra\":         { <locale>: { <namespace>: [\"dotted.key\", ...] } },\n    \"sameAsEnglish\": { <locale>: { <namespace>: [\"dotted.key\", ...] } }\n  }\n\n- `missing`: keys in en/<ns>.json that are intentionally absent from <locale>/<ns>.json (e.g. brand-only labels that should fall through to English).\n- `extra`: keys present in <locale>/<ns>.json that have no English source (e.g. region-specific copy).\n- `sameAsEnglish`: leaf string values that are intentionally identical to the English value. Use cases:\n    1. Brand & product proper nouns: \"QVO\", \"Quality Voice Operations\", \"Federated Ingest\", \"Global Intelligence Network\".\n    2. Third-party product names: \"Salesforce\", \"HubSpot\", \"Google Calendar\", \"Slack\", \"Zapier\".\n    3. Single-word borrowings that legitimately stay in English in the target language (\"Demo\", \"Pro\", \"Workflows\", \"Dashboard\" in German).\n    4. Format strings / placeholders / fixture data: \"Acme Corp\", \"Jane Smith\", \"n={{n}}\", \"© {{year}} Quality Voice Operations\".\n    5. API event names and identifiers: \"call.started\", \"webhook\".\n  Anything not listed here whose non-English value matches the English value byte-for-byte is treated as drift (\"translator forgot to translate this\") and fails CI.\n\nSeed note: the bulk of the entries below are the current state of `client-app/src/locales/{de,es,fr,pt-BR}/{tenant,admin}.json`, which were bootstrapped with English copy and never received a full translation pass. They are listed here so the check runs green today; as proper translations land, the corresponding entries should be removed from this allowlist (the check will then enforce that they stay translated).",
